            "value": "Versión"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Walks, runs, hikes, rides and drives. Tap Start, put your phone away, and Roamr maps the route, speed, time and distance.": {
      "extractionState": "manual",
      "localizations": {
        "es": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "Caminatas, carreras, excursiones, paseos en bici y en auto. Toca Iniciar, guarda el teléfono y Roamr traza la ruta, velocidad, tiempo y distancia."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Week of %@": {
      "extractionState": "manual",
      "localizations": {
        "es": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "Semana del %@"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "While you record a drive, Roamr watches for a sudden jolt with a stop from over 25 mph. It then asks \"Are you OK?\" for 30 seconds and, if you don't answer, opens a text to your emergency contact with your location. iOS doesn't let apps send texts on their own, so someone has to tap Send. This is not a replacement for your iPhone's built-in Crash Detection or for calling 911.": {
      "extractionState": "manual",
      "localizations": {
        "es": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "Mientras grabas un viaje en auto, Roamr vigila un golpe fuerte junto con una frenada desde más de 25 mph. Entonces pregunta \"¿Estás bien?\" durante 30 segundos y, si no respondes, abre un mensaje a tu contacto de emergencia con tu ubicación. iOS no deja que las apps envíen mensajes solas, así que alguien tiene que tocar Enviar. No reemplaza la Detección de choques integrada del iPhone ni llamar al 911."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Without the odometer, Roamr uses the drives it recorded since your last full fill-up.": {
      "extractionState": "manual",
      "localizations": {
        "es": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
